BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 628.00 Tm (Section 4: Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 605.77 Tm (The trap that sinks new operators first is the gap between delivering and getting paid. Giganomic Era warns) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 590.55 Tm (that direct clients pay by invoice, sometimes weeks after the work is done, so a fuel cushion has to exist) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 575.32 Tm (before the first route starts [7Mz5ctFZBX0 @ 00:02:11]. Medical Courier Connection puts harder numbers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 560.10 Tm (on it: purchasing departments stack approval layers, and a contract nobody read closely can mean 90 days) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 544.87 Tm (before the first check lands, with routed work billed at the start of the month and paid in 20-30 days) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 529.65 Tm ([o1VRiVMJTpY @ 00:04:38]. Ken and Linda also lived the credit-card version of this squeeze, funding the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 514.42 Tm (business on plastic and watching 'the best like 900 credit rating' fall to a 400 credit rating in a single year) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 499.20 Tm ([o1VRiVMJTpY @ 00:50:26]. Davis's level-one numbers show the same leak on the app side: a 0.9-mile) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 483.97 Tm (Roadie delivery paid $8, about $1 a mile typical, and unpaid deadhead 'killed it' [9oGonGv8OLc @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 468.75 Tm (00:09:52]. The economics check is blunt. Hold three months of operating expenses, push every client for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 453.52 Tm (ACH, and stack routes so the vehicle earns on every leg, because revenue sitting on an unpaid invoice does) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 438.30 Tm (nothing for a tank that needs filling on Monday morning.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 423.07 Tm (The second cluster of losses comes from paper signed without leverage. Giganomic Era breaks down the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 407.85 Tm (subcontracting math: large-company routes may pay the driver $10 per stop plus a base fee while charging) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 392.62 Tm (the client anywhere from $20 to $50 per stop and double the base [YewfRfz9eUI @ 00:01:26]. The same) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 377.40 Tm (channel flags one-sided termination clauses, where the client can walk immediately while the courier owes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 362.17 Tm (30 days' notice, and tells operators to negotiate rate adjustments and fuel surcharges into the deal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 346.95 Tm ([YewfRfz9eUI @ 00:06:03]. Medical Courier Connection shows what good language is worth: a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 331.72 Tm (pay-the-remainder cancellation clause forced a bank client to pay out roughly eight months after pulling the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 316.50 Tm (work, and charging clients who were free-riding on extras flipped a $35k monthly loss into a $35k monthly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 301.27 Tm (profit [o1VRiVMJTpY @ 00:27:30]. Alton Arell adds a trap that hits before the first contract: Stripe and banks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 286.05 Tm (flag pharmaceutical delivery as high-risk and decline merchant accounts, which is why it is 'utterly important,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 270.82 Tm (extremely important to name your business something neutral' [eOHfnK5euaw @ 00:04:32]. The operator) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 255.60 Tm (takeaway: read every clause, write the client's stated assumptions into the bid, and never let the business) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 240.37 Tm (name or the termination terms hand the client all of the leverage.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 225.15 Tm (Scaling is where firsthand damage stories pile up. Giganomic Era has had drivers destroy and abandon) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 209.92 Tm (vehicles and steal a route outright, which is why that operator now runs MVR checks, background checks, a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 194.70 Tm (ride-along test and a five-day supervised handoff before anyone touches a client stop [2w9s8G4Gx9Q @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 179.47 Tm (00:01:28]. The same channel argues for walking away from routes that clash with day-job hours: 'A missed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 164.25 Tm (opportunity is better than a failed contract that damage your reputation' [7Mz5ctFZBX0 @ 00:06:36]. Michael) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 149.02 Tm (Pacheco frames the structural version of this failure: 'if the foundation isn't right, adding more vehicles can) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 133.80 Tm (simply multiply the problems,' so SOPs have to exist before the fleet grows and the business stops) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 118.57 Tm (depending on the owner [QWuDUoAMiQU @ 00:01:21]. JT Automations reports that lowballers lose bids) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 103.35 Tm (and insists 'You have to offer reliability' when pitching logistics managers [gpeFpvbyWg4 @ 00:12:15]. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 88.12 Tm (economics check on every expansion move comes from the hiring math: a $750-$1,000 weekly route) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 72.90 Tm (stacked with a $500 client only justifies a driver if $300-$500 a week stays with the owner after driver pay.) Tj ET
