BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (plainly: a van is a bill [5gdeSbLFdzk @ 00:08:24]. The WM NEMT Startup Coach host goes further, telling) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (owners not to even research vehicles until the business plan, systems and credit are in place) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm ([TmcbGA0zH6Y @ 00:16:14]. Research means hard local data. Dante at Nemt University has new owners) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (map every competitor inside a roughly 10-mile radius, logging the services they run and their base rates) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm ([sj-P7btgpOQ @ 00:01:20]. Shantasia adds that profitable density matters, because a wide service area) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (turns into empty mileage, and ThatNEMTGirl warns that a broker accepting providers in your state does not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (mean it accepts them in your area, citing Savannah at roughly 4.5 hours from Atlanta. The baseline) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (prerequisite is a validated pocket of demand you can actually reach without burning fuel on deadhead legs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (The second point of near-total agreement is that personal insurance is a trap. Shantasia_RN is direct that a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (personal policy will not cover paid passengers and that even an expired certificate can block trips) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm ([hS8ke40DMr4 @ 00:03:17]. JT Automations spells out the shortcut some newcomers try: claim personal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (use to shave the premium, and the result is a denied claim and a dropped policy [dHKhNi-IC-0 @ 00:11:17].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (Joe Padilla of MediRoutes learned a subtler version firsthand, starting on a commercial Progressive policy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (that still did not cover door-to-door service [g6k_yncRR8o @ 00:17:49]. On limits, ThatNEMTGirl reports) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm ($1M is the most common broker requirement, with some brokers accepting $300K or $500K, and that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (commercial auto plus general liability is the floor [5gdeSbLFdzk @ 00:26:30]. Broker readiness also covers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (optics: brokers check for a website and a professional business phone line. The credential stack repeats) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (speaker to speaker: LLC, EIN, NPI, Medicaid or broker enrollment, background checks and CPR, with drug) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (screening, motor vehicle records and defensive driving layered on for drivers. No medical degree is needed,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (but CPR, vitals and defibrillator training earn respect from brokers. Approval, as Shantasia and Padilla both) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (stress, is a license to compete for trips, not a promise of volume.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (The third consensus is that cash flow, not trip demand, is what kills new owners. NEMT Launch Blueprint) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (frames it bluntly: January trips may not be paid until March, so hold a 60-90 day reserve, because that gap) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm (is what kills new businesses [4_YiCCE47fY @ 00:04:54]. Nemiton pegs Medicaid payment at 30-60 days) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (and tells owners to keep 90 days of cash on hand. Shantasia_RN warns that money in the business account) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.92 Tm (is not automatically owner income and tells operators to reconcile billed versus paid trips before treating any) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.70 Tm (balance as spendable [fWyD2LyLaKE @ 00:06:22]. The same speaker's sharpest line covers concentration) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 274.47 Tm (risk: never confuse having access to trips with owning those trips. Joe Padilla puts dollar figures on that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 259.25 Tm (warning, describing a client running 3,000-4,000 trips a day who had about $1M frozen when a broker went) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 244.02 Tm (bankrupt, and recounts selling a truck for $15K to make payroll [g6k_yncRR8o @ 00:22:49]. Before any) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 228.80 Tm (major move, Shantasia_RN runs a four-question check that includes what happens if revenue arrives late) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 213.57 Tm ([fWyD2LyLaKE @ 00:08:17]. That is why the operators who last stack brokers, facility contracts and private) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 198.35 Tm (pay together, keep lines of credit open, and run the business on reconciled receivables rather than gross) Tj ET
