BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.78 Tm (The broker rate is the first trap operators hit. RouteGenie states flatly that LogistiCare, now Modivcare, does) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.55 Tm (not pay providers for driver wait time at all, and that many small companies opt out because the rates would) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.33 Tm (not let them pay drivers more than minimum wage with no benefits; the broker is paid per member served) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.10 Tm (while providers are paid per trip performed, and that gap is where the broker's profit sits [FBWU2kTGLwI @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 160.88 Tm (00:00:41]. The one lever named is scarcity: if you are one of the only companies in your area providing a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 145.65 Tm (certain service, you have room to negotiate higher prices [FBWU2kTGLwI @ 00:00:59]. ThatNEMTGirl puts) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 130.43 Tm (the volume trap in numbers: ten short ambulatory trips at $35 gross only $350 for the day while burning gas) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 115.20 Tm (and wear and tear, whereas two $250 payouts beat that with less work [govQRXzu6Rg @ 00:02:52]. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 99.98 Tm (same operator warns that long-distance broker calls, an hour to two hours from home base, usually exist) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 84.75 Tm (because somebody else could not do them, so confirm the broker pays dead miles before accepting, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 69.53 Tm (only then run it up [govQRXzu6Rg @ 00:04:44]. Treat any broker trip that ignores wait and dead miles as a) Tj ET
