BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 595.42 Tm (The loudest split is over how dispatch software should be bought and what it really costs. A transportation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 580.20 Tm (lead evaluating platforms for a new two-to-three car fleet walked out of a RouteGenie demo and itemized the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 564.97 Tm (stack: $50 per month per vehicle, a $100 setup fee, 2.5 cents per reminder text, 5 cents per reminder call,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 549.75 Tm (and $250 for one hour of one-on-one training, against Bambi's flat 67 dollars per car with nothing bolted on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 534.52 Tm ([CbCgWxHPCxU @ 00:09:17]. RouteGenie's own pitch takes the opposite posture, bundling up to eight) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 519.30 Tm (training sessions with an implementation specialist, phone and email support through the day, optional) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 504.07 Tm (on-site launch support, and paid customization where time and cost vary per request [j__fVq5xHLo @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 488.85 Tm (00:02:25]. ZeitRide holds at about $50 a month per vehicle and frames it as roughly the cost of a single ride,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 473.62 Tm (while the episode host calls that price very competitive and notes the real decision is per-vehicle versus) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 458.40 Tm (per-volume billing [ajqkD-2jPd8 @ 00:22:24]. SwiftAid Transport's market survey places Bambi around $69) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 443.17 Tm (a month per vehicle for small fleets without an IT department and reserves RouteGenie for the 40-to-50 van) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 427.95 Tm (mid-market, where broker synchronization matters more than interface polish [YGC_f04Hg3g @ 00:21:38].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 412.72 Tm (The operator move is to price the entire fee schedule, not the headline seat rate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 397.50 Tm (Practitioners also split on what a dispatcher should actually be staring at all day. Bambi's team tells) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 382.27 Tm (operators they really do not need the live map, because the color-coded trip boxes on the dispatch calendar) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 367.05 Tm (expand, contract, and change status in real time as drivers tap through the driver app, giving a living view of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 351.82 Tm (the whole fleet at once [mgK4ir9UXtc @ 00:05:04]. RouteGenie argues the reverse priority: seeing every) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 336.60 Tm (vehicle in real time is what lets a dispatcher redirect a driver mid-route around traffic and road conditions) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 321.37 Tm (before a late arrival happens [382JPpV04Tg @ 00:02:13]. MediRoutes sits between the two camps, pairing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 306.15 Tm (a dashboard of every vehicle's location and trip status with a real-time will-call engine that recommends the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 290.92 Tm (best driver by space type, vehicle capacity, proximity, and riders already on board [nLjDVheWODU @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 275.70 Tm (00:05:40]. On optimization, everyone agrees automation beats hand-assignment, but they disagree on how) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 260.47 Tm (far to trust it. Run Bambi Run drafts a full day in under 30 seconds and leaves stretcher trips visibly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 245.25 Tm (unassigned when capacity does not exist, yet Bambi's own knowledge base still has dispatchers build) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 230.02 Tm (multi-loads by hand, enabling multi-loading separately for each payer and manually setting the pickup and) Tj ET
