BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 199.57 Tm (hand-correct multi-loads and exceptions before applying.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 184.35 Tm (The deepest split is over what actually counts as proof of a trip. RouteGenie's August news desk says GPS) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 169.12 Tm (is still essential, but coordinates on their own are not the whole picture: a strong record ties location data to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 153.90 Tm (passenger information, appointments, timestamps, driver activity, credentials, and billing, and the bar is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 138.67 Tm (moving from collecting data to showing that the data tells one consistent story [GWBpqyUYyjE @ 00:02:34].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 123.45 Tm (SwiftAid Transport turns that into a triple match, comparing an audit to a vault that needs three keys turned) Tj ET
